<!--
  Light Gas Cherenkov (LGC): materials, optical property tables and optical surfaces.
  Included by compact/cherenkov/lgc_SIDIS.xml and compact/cherenkov/lgc_PVDIS.xml (only one of them per configuration).
  Every name carries the LGC_ prefix (DD4hep silently ignores duplicate materials/constants).

  Optical tables: verbatim from solid_gemc/geometry/lgc_moved/lg_cherenkov__materials_SIDIS.txt and
  lg_cherenkov__mirrors_SIDIS.txt (identical for PVDIS), generated by a script, 43 photon energies 2.04-6.89 eV
  (606.7-179.9 nm); the reflectivity tables have the first 41 energies (to 6.2 eV) as in GEMC.
  Fixes with respect to GEMC / the old dd4hep compact/optics.xml (see the LGC spec, sections 5 and 9):
    * CO2 RINDEX is the 20 degC table consistent with the 20 degC density (old dd4hep CO2Optical used the 0 degC
      index with the 20 degC density) and has an ABSLENGTH table (old dd4hep: none);
    * PVF windows are C2H3F by atom count (GEMC typed the atom ratio as mass fractions -> 50% H by mass);
    * the mirror blank is CFRP (carbon fiber 65% + epoxy 35% by mass) at the GEMC density 1.8 g/cm3
      (GEMC SL_RCFP had 33% H by mass; old dd4hep used Pyrex glass);
    * UV window: borosilicate composition (GEMC typed atom-like numbers as mass fractions) with the GEMC RINDEX;
    * photocathode: K2CsSb (GEMC: hydrogen at 1 g/cm3) with the CO2 RINDEX as in GEMC (no Fresnel loss on entry);
      the QE table is attached as EFFICIENCY for the digitization (QE is NOT applied in the simulation).
-->
